The game was progressing well. Ninth level Valkyrie, speed boots, gauntlets
of power, Stormbringer, a +4 hard hat and a +3 banded mail found lying in
the dungeon ... things are looking promising for a successful game. A
wand of polymorph is found, and about an hour is spent collecting all manner
of objects ready for a polypile. I have 6 uncursed rocks (identified with
an altar) -- why not throw them in too. Zap the pile and sort through it.
In amongst the splint mails and pronged polearms is 6 gray stones ...
interesting! Obviously the new form of the 6 stones, so they can't be
cursed. Since they are buried under about 50 other items I can't be bothered
moving all the covering junk for the kick test. If they are lodestones,
I can just drop them, since they are uncursed, right! So I duly pick up
the six gray stones. Hmm.. I can still move around OK... why not drop them...
yes, that's right, they won't budge on kicking. Let's pick them up, #name
them for future reference, stick them back on the polypile and have another 
zap. #name n loadstone d v "For some reason you cannot drop the stones!".
What!!!! Evidently loadstones curse on being dropped. No problem, there is
a wand of cancellation on the pile at my feet. "There is a wand of cancellation
here, but you cannot carry any more!" Well, I was going to drop everything
else anyway, so I drop all but Stormie and my worn armor. Same problem again.
Okay, I strip (except for the gauntlets of power), drop my weapon, and try
again. Still no luck! And a big nasty is bearing down on my naked and
defenseless body. Despite recent regular sacrificings (thats how I got Stormie)
all I get is "Loki is pleased." I just wish he would demonstrate it and
uncurse these stones! I can't fight because I can't move, I am unarmoured
and can only engrave with my fingers. Death soon followed.

This may not be a bug, but it was damned annoying! How did I pick up 6 stones
if I couldn't even walk with them? The only positive side to all this
was that a bones level was left, and all the nice stuff will not be cursed.
It had better be me that finds it, though!

One point: this would never have happened if there were a facility to #name
objects that aren't in your pack. How many times have you wished you could
name that emerald potion which just paralysed the monster you threw it at,
but found you couldn't because you didn't have another one?

Dave.


